# {{SolutionName}}

ASP.NET Core Web API generated by **monorepo-dotnet** using a single-project
(1-layer) architecture, Entity Framework Core, {{Database}}{{#if Docker}} and Docker{{/if}}.

## Architecture

```text
{{SolutionName}}/
├── src/
│   └── {{SingleLayerProject}}/
│       ├── Controllers/     # HTTP endpoints
│       ├── Products/        # DTOs, service, validators, MediatR handlers
│       ├── Models/          # Entities
│       ├── Data/            # DbContext, configurations, repositories, migrations
│       └── Program.cs
{{#if Docker}}├── docker-compose.yml
├── Dockerfile
├── .env.example
{{/if}}└── {{SolutionName}}.sln
```

Keep this layout as long as the solution is small. When the project grows,
split it into the DDD or Clean Architecture layout.

## Prerequisites

- .NET SDK {{TargetFramework}} (10.0 or later)
- {{Database}} (local install or Docker)
- `dotnet-ef` tool: `dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef --version {{EfCoreVersion}}`
{{#if Docker}}- Docker Desktop / Docker Engine with Compose v2{{/if}}

## Run with Docker Compose

{{#if Docker}}```bash
docker compose up --build
```

The API is available at `http://localhost:8080`, {{Database}} at
`localhost:{{DatabasePort}}`. `.env` was generated with a random database
password.{{#if SqlServer}} The `{{DatabaseName}}` database is created by the
first migration.{{/if}}
{{/if}}{{#if !Docker}}Docker files were not generated for this solution.
{{/if}}

## Run locally

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
```

```bash
{{#if Postgres}}export ConnectionStrings__Default="Host=localhost;Port={{DatabasePort}};Database={{DatabaseName}};Username={{DatabaseUser}};Password=..."
{{/if}}{{#if SqlServer}}export ConnectionStrings__Default="Server=localhost,{{DatabasePort}};Database={{DatabaseName}};User Id={{DatabaseUser}};TrustServerCertificate=True
Database__Password=..."
{{/if}}dotnet run --project src/{{SingleLayerProject}}
```

## EF Core migrations

```bash
dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate \
  --project src/{{SingleLayerProject}} \
  --startup-project src/{{SingleLayerProject}} \
  --output-dir Data/Migrations

dotnet ef database update \
  --project src/{{SingleLayerProject}} \
  --startup-project src/{{SingleLayerProject}}
```

## API endpoints

| Method | Route | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/health` | Health probe |
| GET | `/api/products` | List products |
| GET | `/api/products/{id}` | Get a product |
| POST | `/api/products` | Create a product |

